Z||000001||FieroMontreal||10-25-2001||08:20 PM||||Not bad, I like em.. but I still think that the Corrado is the sweetest VW..||||reg||1
Z||000002||malacite||10-25-2001||09:03 PM||||i'll admit it. i like volkswagons better than pontiacs. i was originally going to buy a corrado g-60 (supercharged) but the guy sold it before i could get over there.<BR>i couldn't find any scirrocos so #3 was the fiero.<P>for the record #4 is the 1970 chevelle<BR>#5 is the 78 camaro||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||10-25-2001||09:56 PM||||I absolutely love the Corrado as well!  The next car will be either a Corrado VR6, or a CRX Si.  Don't worry, I don't plan on selling my car though...I keep the ones I like <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've seen Sciroccos that looked good, but they had a ton of time invested into them.  I don't think they're worth the effort involved, unless you have a major attraction/dedication to the car.  You can find them very cheap though, that's nice.  Especially if you find a worn out one, they're super cheap.  Not like the Corrado..that cost a TON despite their age (should be though, they are sweet).<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||10-25-2001||11:32 PM||||Scirocco is nice, but I too prefer the Corrado. (the VR6 in my case). <P>VWs are generally bullet-proof reliable and keep their resale like nothing this side of a Honda. <P>I've had 5 VWs so far...<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
